*  earn0_varref_cat_dropped.sno - same defect through a CONCATENATION (2026-08-12 s29).
*  Q = P P is two references to the same pattern-valued variable, so the composite
*  requires TWO subject characters. Subject 'a' is ONE character: SPITBOL says NOMATCH.
*  AT HEAD fc5b0754 SCRIP PRINTS 'MATCH' rc=0 -- both references read as null, so the
*  composite degenerates to the null pattern.
*  IR EVIDENCE: `P = LEN(1)` lowers to an EMPTY STATEMENT (no ASSIGN emitted at all) and
*  the composite lowers to a plain BINOP binop=11 concat over VAR P operands.
*  ⛔ SILENT CLASS: exit code 0, plausible output, no crash. The corpus cannot see it.
*  ⛔⭐ s29 MASK WARNING: under SCRIP_PAT_INLINE=0 this stops printing a wrong answer and
*  HANGS instead (rc=0 -> rc=124). The silent wrong answer was MASKING a broken consumer
*  path (DEFECT B). FIXING THE ELISION ALONE WILL LOOK LIKE A REGRESSION HERE.
*  Judge BY SET; expect the hang count to RISE when defect A is fixed. That is the mask
*  coming off, not new damage. Run the MONITOR at the DEFAULT arm -- it terminates there.
        P = LEN(1)
        Q = P P
        'a' Q                                    :S(Y)F(N)
Y       OUTPUT = 'MATCH'                         :(D)
N       OUTPUT = 'NOMATCH'
D       OUTPUT = 'DONE'
END
